am, we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(D)=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 3\\cdot 6=9.\n$$\n\nComputing the determinant of $T,$ we get \n\n$$\ndet(T)=3\\cdot 4-2\\cdot 2=8.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(D)) & =|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =|\\,8\\,|\\cdot 9 \\\\  & =72.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186303273 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a51f9b53-0ce5-518f-8173-abe4d87f2851" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area of the Image of an Object Under a Linear Transformation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a4ae30c6-ac05-575a-b0f4-76a7ab7caef4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "48" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303275}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a4ae30c6-ac05-575a-b0f4-76a7ab7caef4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "48" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303275} :answer-field/id #uuid "4f393b8e-2297-5b65-897e-ea43622fccaa" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303274}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "215b2454-d24f-559c-8109-17676c571bcc" :question/math-academy-id "q-275983" :question/problem "The triangle $D$ has vertices $(2,2),(4,6),(6,2).$ What is the area of the image of $D$ under the action of the linear transformation $T$ with the standard matrix $T,$ given below?\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n$\\text{Area}(T(D))=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, let's sketch our region:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039564/assets/a4e507191aecd02e16fafba29598972df423e975dd554b260ca355f0cf6476a1.png)\n\nRecall that for any linear transformation $T,$ we have the following connection between the area of $D$ and the area of the image $T(D)$ under the action of $T:$\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(T(D))=|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D).\n$$\n\nFrom the diagram, we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(D)=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 4\\cdot 4=8.\n$$\n\nComputing the determinant of $T,$ we get \n\n$$\ndet(T)=1\\cdot 0-3\\cdot (-2)=6.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(D)) & =|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =|\\,6\\,|\\cdot 8 \\\\  & =48.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186303279 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "80a4eee7-a763-5c28-ae3c-5bce78222c87" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Area Scale Factor of a Linear Transformation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "16e1b40d-5e5a-5e30-89c8-edac91f58529" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "89" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303281} {:answer/id #uuid "3831a940-666b-51f6-878e-71b88512ceae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-89" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303282}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "16e1b40d-5e5a-5e30-89c8-edac91f58529" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "89" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303281} :answer-field/id #uuid "182ce720-e152-57eb-9369-c8490a44193b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303280}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "182ce155-065c-526e-891c-1c2103b06de4" :question/math-academy-id "q-316569" :question/problem "What is the area scale factor of the linear transformation $T$ that is given by its standard matrix \n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}-10 & 9 \\\\ 1 & 8\\end{aligned}]?\n$$\n\nThe area scale factor is\n{{field-1}} ." :question/worked-solution "The area scale factor of a linear transformation $T$ with standard matrix $T$ is equal to $|det(T)|.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|det(T)| & =|-10\\cdot 8-9\\cdot 1| \\\\  & =|-80-9| \\\\  & =|-89| \\\\  & =89.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 