=1\\cdot 2-(-1)\\cdot 2=4.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(D)) & =|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =|\\,4\\,|\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =24.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284000 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4d59733f-3396-5d59-98a9-3f2e0ccfbbc4" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area of the Image of an Object Under a Linear Transformation Given a Diagram"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "eba14f18-bf0d-54e8-a07d-3286887fc85d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284002} {:answer/id #uuid "b86bf782-71e0-5762-8b4b-387022dd5096" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284003}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b86bf782-71e0-5762-8b4b-387022dd5096" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284003} :answer-field/id #uuid "fc1d744e-1f26-5a9d-b352-65582ed7f9bc" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284001}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "75101661-a27e-5e03-93ec-d54f3d950523" :question/math-academy-id "q-316588" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13992537/assets/cec4f46a70e55735e07cc77fb2013c8d5262ca15feda1ee9eac005a79d38147d.png)\n\nConsider the shaded region $D$ shown above. What is the area of the image of $D$ under the action of the linear transformation $T$ with the standard matrix $T,$ given below?\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n$\\text{Area}(T(D))=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Recall that for any linear transformation $T,$ we have the following connection between the area of $D$ and the area of the image $T(D)$ under the action of $T:$\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(T(D))=|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D).\n$$\n\nFrom the diagram, we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(D)=\\frac{1}{2}\\,(4+2)\\cdot 2=6.\n$$\n\nComputing the determinant of $T,$ we get \n\n$$\ndet(T)=(-1)\\cdot (-2)-(-2)\\cdot 1=4.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(D)) & =|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =|\\,4\\,|\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =24.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186291904 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a51f9b53-0ce5-518f-8173-abe4d87f2851" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area of the Image of an Object Under a Linear Transformation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "81001409-c569-533a-a2b7-efcf7f397e46" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291906}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "81001409-c569-533a-a2b7-efcf7f397e46" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291906} :answer-field/id #uuid "f259a8c8-cae9-5672-86ca-ce9c8aca1649" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291905}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "75fce5ef-ce16-54b6-beee-1ddbfa19c810" :question/math-academy-id "q-316598" :question/problem "The unit square $D$ has vertices $(1,0),(0,0),(0,1),(1,1).$ What is the area of the image of $D$ under the action of the linear transformation $T$ with the standard matrix $T,$ given below?\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n$\\text{Area}(T(D))=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, let's sketch our region:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014125/assets/6805467a24cb40559f205cbfcecc4f5a34ff2ec6ebda8ae67f997c02f123b53c.png)\n\nRecall that for any linear transformation $T,$ we have the following connection between the area of $D$ and the area 