jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13992537/assets/92ee29a22baa10f4af25db8221e7d67c729f5f0f1b5e1b3c37aee7e31a92bdfb.png)\n\nRecall that for any linear transformation $T,$ we have the following connection between the area of $D$ and the area of the image $T(D)$ under the action of $T:$\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(T(D))=|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D).\n$$\n\nFrom the diagram, we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(D)=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 4\\cdot 3=6.\n$$\n\nComputing the determinant of $T,$ we get \n\n$$\ndet(T)=4\\cdot 1-1\\cdot (-3)=4+3=7.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(D)) & =|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =|\\,7\\,|\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =42.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
